WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.334
-Welcome. Thank you.

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:05.300
-That is about an amazing band
that makes you want to dance.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.334
-That's exactly right.

00:00:06.334 --> 00:00:07.767
-Shout out to the band.

00:00:07.767 --> 00:00:09.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.334 --> 00:00:10.567
-Welcome to the show.

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:13.300
You've recently been named
E's red carpet host.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.100
-Yes.
-This is -- this is a big deal.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:16.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yes.

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:17.901
-This is a big deal.

00:00:17.901 --> 00:00:22.067
-We -- it's such an honor and
I'm having such a good time.

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:24.667
we just did the People's Choice
Awards a few months ago

00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:26.934
and on Sunday, we're doing
the Screen Actors Guild Awards,

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:29.434
the S.A.G. Awards.
And I love artists.

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:31.701
I love actors. The S.A.G.
Awards are always so much fun,

00:00:31.701 --> 00:00:33.968
and it is star-studded.

00:00:33.968 --> 00:00:36.267
When I got the list of
the people I'm potentially

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:37.834
interviewing, I was like --
[ Gasps ]

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:39.934
I really had a gasp,
but I was like,

00:00:39.934 --> 00:00:41.734
"I need to really get it
together."

00:00:41.734 --> 00:00:43.534
Because they're names like --
-Who are you excited about?

00:00:43.534 --> 00:00:45.267
-People like Leonardo DiCaprio.
-Uh-huh.

00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:47.901
-Like, if you're an actor,
and Leonardo DiCaprio is,

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:50.000
like, [emphatically] an actor.
-Yeah.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.400
-Denzel Washington is
[emphatically] an actor.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.367
-Yeah, he's unbelievable.
Yeah.

00:00:54.367 --> 00:00:55.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.467 --> 00:00:57.868
-Cate Blanchett --
"Cate the Great."

00:00:57.868 --> 00:00:59.801
-No. "Cate the Great,"
she's unbelievable.

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:01.734
-It's fun, though,
because it's two hours.

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:03.467
I realized the day of,
I was like,

00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:05.567
"I can't go to the bathroom.
I can't leave."

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:06.901
I have to be on the red carpet
for two hours.

00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:09.267
So I stopped all liquids
at 2:00 P.M.

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:10.334
-That's smart.
-Because the red carpet starts

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:11.367
at 6:00.
-Very smart.

00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:12.767
-And you're there
the whole time,

00:01:12.767 --> 00:01:14.200
and there's all this stuff
coming at you, but you have to

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.501
be on your toes and be on --
think on your feet.

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:17.868
And anything can happen,

00:01:17.868 --> 00:01:19.767
and that's actually really fun
and exciting.

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:23.501
-You've had a bunch of jobs,
but this one I read about

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:24.834
and it made me laugh because
I go,

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:26.734
"I don't know if
I remember this."

00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:28.367
But I remember the show,
kind of.

00:01:28.367 --> 00:01:30.601
Was it like, "I Will Work for
Diddy," or something?

00:01:30.601 --> 00:01:32.334
Or --
-"I Want to Work for Diddy."

00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:35.200
I was on -- in 2008,
I did a reality show

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.501
called "I Want to Work for
Diddy."

00:01:36.501 --> 00:01:38.734
-I remember the show.
-It was my phase of saying "yes"

00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:40.167
to everything.
-Yeah.

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:42.300
-[ Laughs ]
-Did you want to work for Diddy?

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.601
-No, girl.

00:01:43.601 --> 00:01:44.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.801 --> 00:01:46.834
No. It was an --

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:48.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:50.100
[ Cymbal crashes ]

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:53.434 --> 00:01:55.667
-That's it. I don't know.

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:57.000
I can't take that.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.667
-It was an -- it was an
opportunity to be on television.

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:03.767
This was 2008, so, like,
a transperson had never been

00:02:03.767 --> 00:02:05.734
on a competition reality show
in 2008.

00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:06.868
-Yeah.
-It was about building

00:02:06.868 --> 00:02:08.133
relationships with
the casting director.

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:10.300
I didn't really want to do it,
but they loved me.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:12.534
And I think I -- because
I didn't care, I went in,

00:02:12.534 --> 00:02:14.868
I was myself.
And the interesting of them --

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:16.167
there are so many interesting
things that happened

00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:18.567
on that show, but because
I had watched "Making the Band,"

00:02:18.567 --> 00:02:21.534
I knew that Diddy would wake you
up in the middle of the night

00:02:21.534 --> 00:02:24.033
to do stuff, and I was like,
"I do not want to be

00:02:24.033 --> 00:02:25.968
on national television without
my makeup

00:02:25.968 --> 00:02:27.367
at 2:00 in the morning."

00:02:27.367 --> 00:02:31.534
So, at night, I would wash all
my makeup off, reapply it,

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:32.767
and then go to sleep.

00:02:32.767 --> 00:02:34.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.434 --> 00:02:35.634
-See? That's how you do it.

00:02:35.634 --> 00:02:37.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
-And sure enough --

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.033
-Genius.
-The second challenge,

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:41.868
we were wakened at, like,
2:00 or 3:00 in the morning,

00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:44.033
and I woke up, and I was like,
"Yes."

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:45.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.501 --> 00:02:47.000
-And here you are now.
-Yes.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:50.501
-Here you are now. I want to
talk about "inventing Anna" too.

00:02:50.501 --> 00:02:52.434
-Oh, my God.
- You're doing it great, though.

00:02:52.434 --> 00:02:53.901
Everyone is crushing
on the show.

00:02:53.901 --> 00:02:55.033
It's -- congrats,
number one show on Netflix.

00:02:55.033 --> 00:02:56.934
-Thank you. Thank you.
-Not too bad.

00:02:56.934 --> 00:02:58.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:00.367
Number one show on Netflix.

00:03:00.367 --> 00:03:02.601
But your character is based on
a real person.

00:03:02.601 --> 00:03:05.601
-Yes. I play --
so "Inventing Anna" is about

00:03:05.601 --> 00:03:08.334
this woman named Anna Delvey,
AKA Anna Sorokin,

00:03:08.334 --> 00:03:12.033
who is a fake heiress who conned
the New York social scene

00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:13.834
several years ago.
It's based on a true story.

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:15.634
And I play a woman named
Kacy Duke, who was her

00:03:15.634 --> 00:03:17.467
personal trainer
and she's a life coach.

00:03:17.467 --> 00:03:20.434
And I got to meet Kacy.
She trained me.

00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:22.133
I had a four hour lunch with her

00:03:22.133 --> 00:03:23.367
where she told me
her life story.

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:24.834
She lived this incredible life.

00:03:24.834 --> 00:03:26.000
She's -- Speaking of
Denzel Washington,

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.868
she trained everyone from
Denzel Washington

00:03:27.868 --> 00:03:30.501
to Lenny Kravitz
to Julianne Moore.

00:03:30.501 --> 00:03:33.834
And she's been in the business
for, you know, over 30 years.

00:03:33.834 --> 00:03:36.968
She's a legend. And she's
this really spiritual woman

00:03:36.968 --> 00:03:38.400
who is incredible.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.801
And she got, sort of, roped into
this crazy, crazy scheme --

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:43.767
-What does she think
of your performance?

00:03:43.767 --> 00:03:46.834
-She has been so ama--
and I was so nervous.

00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:48.934
I was, like,
really in so much anxiety.

00:03:48.934 --> 00:03:50.501
Because I was like, "Oh, my God.
if Kacy hates it,

00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:51.601
this is going to be terrible."

00:03:51.601 --> 00:03:53.801
But she sent me
the sweetest message.

00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:56.267
She sent me flowers.
She said, "Congratulations.

00:03:56.267 --> 00:03:58.234
Laverne is killing it."

00:03:58.234 --> 00:03:59.634
-Aww.
-She has been so sweet.

00:03:59.634 --> 00:04:02.000
And a friend of hers tweeted me.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.033
They said -- they were like,
"I've known Kacy Duke

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:07.501
for 20 years
and Laverne Cox nailed it."

00:04:07.501 --> 00:04:09.300
And I was like, "Oh, my God."
-That's all you need.

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:11.067
-Yeah.
-That's all you need, right?

00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:12.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:14.968
-It's a great show.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:14.968 --> 00:04:17.367
Here's Laverne Cox
in "Inventing Anna."

00:04:17.367 --> 00:04:18.701
Take a look.

00:04:18.701 --> 00:04:21.667
-She is out there by a pool
while I am here dodging

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:23.534
calls from my credit card
company.

00:04:23.534 --> 00:04:26.234
-I heard if you legally change
your name,

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:28.267
they can't make you pay that.

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:31.133
But chill. She'll know.

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:34.501
-Easy for you to chill,
she paid you back.

00:04:34.501 --> 00:04:36.734
And how are you so calm
right now?

00:04:36.734 --> 00:04:39.200
-I'm just not letting Anna
take anything more from me.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:42.000
No more of my time.
No more of my attention.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.968
-I wish I had your zen.
You're not angry at all.

00:04:44.968 --> 00:04:47.000
-Here's the thing about anger.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.634
When you're angry,
you're just a character

00:04:49.634 --> 00:04:51.901
in someone else's story.

00:04:51.901 --> 00:04:57.000
But when you let your anger go,
you reclaim your own story,

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:00.400
become your own protagonist
again.

00:05:00.934 --> 00:05:02.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Laverne Cox!

00:05:02.534 --> 00:05:04.200
Check out "Inventing Anna,"

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:05.801
which is streaming now
on Netflix.

